ebb7683@venus.tamu.edu (Ed Blackman) writes:

>My roommate and I both have the latest version of Nethack (3.1.3), both
>obtained in binary form from linc.cis.upenn.edu.  I run OS/2, and he runs 
>DOS.  Can we safely exchange bones files, or are the OS/2 and DOS bones 
>file formats incompatible?

While I won't say this is the definitive answer, I don't think you will
have any problem swapping files. I'm playing ver 3.1.3 under the following
conditions.  Have a boot manager under OS/2 2.1 which boots either O/S 2
on my E: drive (HPFS) or DOS on my D: drive (FAT).  Nethack is on my DOS
drive.  When I start OS/2, my STARTUP.CMD file runs CHKDSK/F on the DOS
drive to update the extended attributes for my DOS programs.  I believe
that I have saved many a game in both DOS and OS/2 and play NETHACK under
both operating systems without any known problems.  My E: (plus c:) and D:
drives are two seperate hard drives.

When I first went to migrate my DOS and WINDOWS programs on D: into OS/2,
the only files it found were some DOS commands and NETHACK!  Only after
running CHKDSK/F D: from within OS/2, did the migration program find all my
other DOS and WINDOWS programs. This says something about NETHACK, but I'm
not sure what. 



